       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient would be at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and arrhythmia.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the maximum dose.\n\nIf 1000 mg is intentional, for example because of a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
